WEBVTT

00:09:28.966 --> 00:09:30.117
who was at Chicago,

00:09:30.141 --> 00:09:32.964
and I thought a lot about one question
his work poses to us.

00:09:32.988 --> 00:09:35.293
Professor Cacioppo asked,

00:09:35.317 --> 00:09:36.967
"Why do we exist?

00:09:36.991 --> 00:09:38.944
Why are we here, why are we alive?"

00:09:38.968 --> 00:09:41.174
One key reason

00:09:41.198 --> 00:09:44.015
is that our ancestors
on the savannas of Africa

00:09:44.039 --> 00:09:45.759
were really good at one thing.

00:09:46.287 --> 00:09:49.577
They weren't bigger than the animals
they took down a lot of the time,

00:09:49.601 --> 00:09:52.914
they weren't faster than the animals
they took down a lot of the time,

00:09:52.938 --> 00:09:55.652
but they were much better
at banding together into groups

00:09:55.676 --> 00:09:57.276
and cooperating.

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.561
This was our superpower as a species --

00:09:59.585 --> 00:10:00.990
we band together,